Task: In a magical world, different spells perform unique actions when cast. Your task is to implement polymorphism by overriding the `cast()` method in the `FireballSpell` and `HealSpell` classes. Ensure each spell announces its specific effect when cast.

Submitted code:
```
class Spell {
  constructor(name) {
    this.name = name;
  }

  cast() {
    return `${this.name} is cast! (Generic effect)`;
  }
}

class FireballSpell extends Spell {
  constructor(damage) {
    super("Fireball");
    this.damage = damage;
  }

  // TODO: Override the cast method to describe the Fireball's specific effect.
  // It should mention the 'damage' amount.
  cast() {
    return "Fireball does" + this.damage + " damage."; // Implement specific effect here
  }
}

class HealSpell extends Spell {
  constructor(healingAmount) {
    super("Heal");
    this.healingAmount = healingAmount;
  }

  // TODO: Override the cast method to describe the Heal spell's specific effect.
  // It should mention the 'healingAmount'.
  cast() {
    return "Healing does " + this.healingAmount + " healing."; // Implement specific effect here
  }
}

```

